<title>USA: TABLE - Xomed Surgical Q2 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Xomed Surgical Q2 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSONVILLE, Fla. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr profit		  $0.18     loss	 $0.89</p>
<p> Net profit		  1,327     loss	 3,592</p>
<p> Revs			 19,203		   16,634</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    7,477		    4,623</p>
<p>			First half</p>
<p> Shr profit		  $0.32     loss	 $0.83</p>
<p> Net profit		  2,414     loss	 3,215</p>
<p> Revs			 37,007		   32,942</p>
<p> Avg shrs		    7,458		    4,620</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name of company Xomed Surgical Products Inc.</p>
<p>Company said it had &quot;adjusted&quot; 1996 Q2 profit $644,000, or $0.14/shr, which exclude charges below and results on a proforma basis.</p>
<p>1996 losses include pretax write-off of acquired research of $2,380,000 and restructuring charges of $3,093,000. Loss per share after preferred stock dividends of $539,000 in both periods.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
